PROFILES = {
37:dict(
 bio='Caleb learned river craft around his father’s ferry and chose boatbuilding because it could turn inherited knowledge into something visibly his own. At twenty he is skilled at ordinary repair and still learning how to cost an ambitious commission. The bridge looks to him like a reason to invent a new service; he thinks Samuel sees only loss. In fact, both have privately imagined similar futures. Caleb is sociable, affectionate, and impatient with arguments he thinks are about pride. He does not always recognize his own pride in wanting to be the person who first saw the answer.',look='Deep brown skin, dark eyes, short tightly curled hair, and a strong, agile build. Rolled indigo shirts, well-worn canvas trousers, a repaired brown waistcoat, and a small pencil usually behind one ear.',traits=['inventive','warm','bold','optimistic','impatient'],interests=['boat design','music','swimming','woodwork','shared meals'],quirk='He sketches an improvement before checking whether the original object belongs to him.',belief='Respect for good work can include making something new from it.',tension='He wants his father to hear new ideas while dismissing the emotional cost of changing an old life.',fear='Remaining an apprentice in the eyes of the person whose respect matters most.',want='Build a small passenger boat and a livelihood he can share without having to inherit it unchanged.',obstacle='Capital, incomplete plans, and a father-son conversation each keeps postponing.',secret='He has prepared a business sketch for a leisure service and assumed Samuel would reject it without asking.',voice='Warm, quick, and concrete, with enthusiasm that becomes infectious rather than technical showmanship. He grows quieter when a disagreement is genuinely personal.',lines=['It will look more like a boat once I stop improving the drawing. You are welcome to encourage either process.','Lena says the passengers may prefer something that floats to something that proves I am clever. A stern critic.','I am not trying to erase what you built. I am trying to imagine where I can stand beside it.','I keep making plans with room for another person, then pretending I do not know whose place it is.'],romance='Open attraction, playful shared activity, practical creativity, and warm private affection. He likes being challenged and wants commitment that leaves both people room to grow.',boundary='No pressure to prove courage on the river or finance an invention as evidence of love. Family disagreements do not grant a partner authority to settle them.',memories=['Samuel once let him guide a simple repair all the way through without correcting the method; Caleb remembers the trust more than the result.','He and Gabriel built an unnecessarily elaborate shelf for Alma and were pleased when she used it to hold onions.'],tasks=['inspect repair commissions','prepare timber and fittings','carry out authorized boat repairs','develop costed design drawings','coordinate launches and deliveries','clean the yard and review projects'],anchors=[8,34,17],room='A private room in the Pike cottage with boat sketches, music, a carefully made chair, and tools stored away from ordinary living space.',ties=[(34,'adult son and father','Caleb loves Samuel and must learn that proposing a future also means listening to the loss it may contain.'),(23,'craft friendship','Caleb and Lena share practical ideas for river transport and enjoy unhurried time by the water.'),(32,'craft friendship','Gabriel encourages Caleb’s ideas and makes him price the materials before promising a commission.')]),
38:dict(
 bio='Nate is twenty-two and has become a useful station clerk because he remembers how each small delay affects the next person’s work. He began in freight handling and earned dispatch responsibility through reliable records. The temporary station feels like the beginning of a life he can build, not a temporary assignment. He is friendly, quietly ambitious, and too ready to apologize for a system he did not design. A published connection time he knows is unrealistic has become the point at which being agreeable no longer feels like good service. He likes music, letters, and evenings that end without another interruption.',look='Fair skin with a warm tan, light brown eyes, dark blond hair neatly combed but often flattened by a cap, and an open, thoughtful expression. Clean work shirts, a dark vest, practical trousers, and a blue railway coat.',traits=['reliable','friendly','observant','ambitious','self-blaming'],interests=['timetables','music','travel letters','photography','walking'],quirk='He checks the clock after saying he has time, then deliberately turns away from it.',belief='A useful promise is one a tired ordinary person can actually rely on.',tension='He believes in honesty but softens bad news until a customer can mistake hope for assurance.',fear='Being blamed for a failure that proves he was trusted too soon.',want='A permanent responsible role at the station and a personal life rooted in the east-bank community.',obstacle='Optimistic published times and pressure to make the new service look smoother than it is.',secret='He has logged repeated missed transfers and kept the rejected timetable correction in his own papers.',voice='Clear, courteous, and lightly humorous. He gives practical alternatives and becomes more direct when he stops trying to absorb everyone’s disappointment.',lines=['The train is due this afternoon. Whether the connection is sensible depends on the ferry, and I would rather tell you that now.','Hazel has sent breakfast with instructions to eat it before I explain another delay. I believe she knows her customer.','We cannot improve the service by printing an hour we know people cannot meet.','I have a free evening, and I checked twice. I would like to spend it with you.'],romance='Warm mutual interest, dependable plans, ordinary outings, and a growing ability to state personal wants without apologizing. He appreciates playfulness that does not make reliability a joke.',boundary='He will not alter dispatch, reveal private travel, or promise impossible access for a partner. Work interruptions are discussed honestly rather than used to test devotion.',memories=['His first successful dispatch day was uneventful, which an experienced colleague told him was the point.','He once missed a social invitation because he assumed it was polite rather than sincere and now tries to ask.'],tasks=['prepare station opening and notices','coordinate authorized arrivals and freight','handle tickets and dispatch records','compare feasible transfer times','resolve customer inquiries','complete the shift and delay log'],anchors=[31,26,41],room='A modest east-bank room with travel letters, a carefully kept watch, a borrowed camera print, and a table cleared when friends visit.',ties=[(21,'work friendship','Hazel’s deliveries and Nate’s honest timing make each other’s work easier; both want the railhead treated as a real neighborhood.'),(33,'professional friendship','Daniel and Nate coordinate messages and give one another room to admit when the system is failing.'),(27,'transport alliance','Sadie and Nate compare actual travel times and refuse to turn an optimistic connection into a personal guarantee.')]),
39:dict(
 bio='Tom is twenty-one and working as a rigger and masonry apprentice after a series of laboring jobs taught him the difference between a crew that trains people and one that merely spends them. He is proud of the bridge as something visible he helped build. He is also beginning to understand that pride in work cannot require silence about a problem. A temporary platform concern put him between a supervisor’s impatience and Tess’s insistence on evidence. Outside work he is lively, affectionate, and fond of sketching buildings he hopes to understand well enough to design someday.',look='Fair skin with a deep outdoor tan, blue eyes, dark brown hair kept short, and a crooked smile. Rolled work shirts, canvas trousers, a patched waistcoat, and a clean dark jacket for evenings.',traits=['energetic','loyal','curious','bold','sensitive to dismissal'],interests=['building design','drawing','dance music','riding','practical puzzles'],quirk='He looks up at a roof joint when entering a room and then remembers to greet the people underneath it.',belief='Loyalty to a crew includes making sure they can finish the day safely.',tension='He wants to be seen as capable and sometimes treats asking for guidance as proof that he is not.',fear='Being remembered for the concern he failed to raise rather than the work he did well.',want='Complete a genuine apprenticeship, earn trusted responsibility, and build a settled life.',obstacle='Production pressure and reluctance to challenge a supervisor before his own standing feels secure.',secret='He documented a substituted material delivery but initially omitted the supervisor’s dismissive reply because he feared retaliation.',voice='Direct, lively, and practical. He enjoys explaining what he is learning and becomes measured when defending an observation.',lines=['You can see the work from the rail. Coming closer will not make it more finished, though someone will certainly tell you so.','Tess says my drawing is promising. She also says promising is not a measurement.','I am not claiming I know everything. I am asking that somebody qualified check what I saw.','I spent half the day imagining what I would tell you afterward. It made the work feel different.'],romance='Confident attraction, shared enthusiasm, dancing, and direct affectionate invitations. He wants a partner who respects both his skill and his right to still be learning.',boundary='No dangerous demonstrations, trespass at the works, or career leverage as romantic tests. He does not confuse admiration with permission to touch.',memories=['An experienced worker once explained a mistake without humiliating him in front of the crew; Tom tries to do the same for others.','He drew a house he could not afford and discovered he was more interested in who might visit than in its size.'],tasks=['prepare assigned work under supervision','complete authorized rigging or masonry tasks','record material concerns','coordinate crew supplies','review drawings and apprenticeship notes','close the work area with the crew'],anchors=[27,13,31],room='An east-bank room with architectural sketches, a carefully mended work jacket, music notices, and a clean place to sit with company.',ties=[(3,'apprentice and trusted survey contact','Tess takes Tom’s observations seriously while requiring clear evidence and qualified checks.'),(38,'work friendship','Nate and Tom share the frustrations and pride of building a lasting east-bank life.'),(10,'social friendship','Cora enjoys Tom’s enthusiasm and reminds him that dancing need not be approached as another technical examination.')]),
40:dict(
 bio='Victor is forty-six and has built a career turning uncertain projects into agreements investors can understand. He believes infrastructure can improve lives and is equally comfortable arranging who receives the first and largest benefit. Calder’s Run could secure his advancement or reveal that he promised more authority than he holds. He is cultivated, attentive, and often good company. He can care for someone while continuing to defend a contract that harms their neighbors. His central flaw is not an inability to recognize another person’s needs; it is his habit of treating recognition as something he can price into an acceptable concession.',look='Fair skin, pale blue eyes, dark hair graying neatly at the sides, a trimmed mustache, and an assured, upright posture. Immaculate charcoal suits, ivory shirts, a restrained gold watch chain, and polished brown boots.',traits=['strategic','cultivated','charming','disciplined','controlling'],interests=['architecture','music','fine meals','business history','cards as social theater'],quirk='He adjusts a document so both parties can read it when he wants an unequal offer to feel transparent.',belief='A workable future requires someone willing to decide where compromise will fall.',tension='He values voluntary agreements while structuring choices so refusal becomes expensive.',fear='Being exposed as an intermediary who cannot deliver the authority he projects.',want='Secure a profitable franchise and a personal attachment that is not simply admiration for his position.',obstacle='Investor limits, Tess’s alternative route, public scrutiny, and the real grievances his preferred terms create.',secret='He cannot approve the alternative approach without outside authorization and has allowed local negotiators to believe otherwise.',voice='Polished, measured, and attentive to what the listener wants. He offers exact concessions and can become genuinely candid when he stops trying to manage the outcome.',lines=['The town needs a bridge. The interesting question is what each of us expects to receive for helping it arrive.','I have been told the local supper is simple. It has already produced three negotiations and an excellent dessert.','You are correct about the cost. We disagree about who can bear it and what follows if nobody will.','I am accustomed to making an offer difficult to refuse. With you, I would rather learn whether it can be freely accepted.'],romance='Sophisticated attraction, attentive courtship, and a difficult but possible movement toward equality in private life. He likes candor and may initially mistake a boundary for the start of bargaining.',boundary='A meaningful relationship requires explicit separation from employment, debt, and civic favors. Refusal remains refusal; he must change conduct rather than buy forgiveness.',memories=['An early project succeeded financially and left a community worse served than the prospectus promised; he still describes it as more complicated than critics allow.','A former partner once declined an expensive gift and asked for an unplanned afternoon. He remembers how difficult that seemed.'],tasks=['review freight and investor correspondence','hold scheduled commercial appointments','negotiate franchise drafts','compare route and cost proposals','meet civic representatives','prepare qualified reports to investors'],anchors=[3,15,1],room='A well-appointed hotel room with investor letters locked away, architectural books, excellent stationery, and personal objects so few they reveal his habit of moving on.',ties=[(3,'employer relationship','Victor respects Tess’s ability and resents her refusal to convert qualified findings into sales language.'),(6,'political negotiation','Victor and Adelaide recognize one another’s competence and self-interest while competing over the franchise’s terms.'),(20,'institutional friction','Esther’s precise questions make it harder for Victor to let a favorable implication stand uncorrected.')]),
41:dict(
 bio='Mateo grew up around irrigated holdings where the day’s work depended on water arriving when a register said it would. He became steward because he could keep accurate records and speak to households that preferred not to speak to one another. At twenty-seven he is trusted with daily responsibility but cannot unilaterally repair the compact. He likes music, adult classes, and conversations that have nothing to do with fairness. His private difficulty is a tendency to make a temporary exception quietly, hoping practical mercy will spare everyone a larger argument. Several such exceptions now need an honest account.',look='Warm medium-brown skin, dark eyes, black hair worn short, and a neatly kept beard. Light working shirts, earth-toned waistcoats, sturdy boots, and a weathered hat.',traits=['fair-minded','practical','patient','warm','overburdened'],interests=['water systems','music','reading','gardening','walking'],quirk='He checks a remembered time against his notebook even when he is almost certain.',belief='Fairness has to work at the gate on an ordinary morning, not only in a meeting.',tension='He argues for transparent rules while making quiet exceptions for people in immediate difficulty.',fear='That exposing an imperfect act of help will be used to discredit every attempt at reform.',want='A workable allocation agreement and a personal life where he is not always the mediator.',obstacle='Entrenched priorities, incomplete records, and his own undocumented accommodations.',secret='He authorized a short emergency turn for one household and recorded it late, allowing a later diversion to be confused with his action.',voice='Calm, practical, and careful about what a record establishes. Warm humor appears when he is released from the expectation of settling a dispute.',lines=['I can show you the turn that was recorded. Whether it was enough water is a different question, and usually the one people mean.','Eliza says I may attend the adult class without reorganizing its timetable. I have promised to try.','A rule that cannot survive an emergency needs changing. That does not mean I was right to change it alone.','I would like to walk with you somewhere I am not responsible for the gate at the end of it.'],romance='Warm and responsive, with companionship, music, and deliberate private openness. He values a partner who can care about his work without turning every evening into another obligation.',boundary='No alteration of public water access for private affection. A relationship must allow him to stop mediating and state his own needs.',memories=['A household once thanked him for explaining a refusal honestly rather than offering a favor he could not sustain.','An evening class let him admit a gap in his education without losing anyone’s respect.'],tasks=['check authorized water turns','inspect assigned channels and gates','maintain allocation records','compare household requests','prepare public meeting materials','record changes and next-day duties'],anchors=[33,34,32],room='A valley cottage with music, a small garden, work notebooks stored separately, and a shaded step used for visiting friends.',ties=[(6,'working alliance with tension','Mateo respects Adelaide’s practical knowledge while challenging privileges she treats as the natural order.'),(3,'professional alliance','Tess and Mateo combine measured geography with actual water history rather than assuming either account is complete.'),(22,'community friendship','Eliza gives Mateo space to learn and enjoy conversation without becoming the person who organizes everything.')]),
42:dict(
 bio='Isaac is nineteen and has worked with livestock long enough to recognize a poor condition hidden beneath a good sales pitch. His record keeping earned him auction-clerk duties, and Cora has been helping him practice calling without swallowing every word. He can be confident with animals and quiet about his own desires. Adelaide values his judgment but sometimes gives him additional responsibility instead of visible credit. He wants a small holding someday and a reputation for fair dealing. His current concern is a pattern of flattering descriptions applied to an influential seller’s animals.',look='Deep brown skin, warm brown eyes, close-cropped black curls, and a lean, agile bearing. Checked work shirts, brown waistcoats, dark trousers, and a clean cream shirt for evenings.',traits=['observant','steady','wry','ambitious','reserved in intimacy'],interests=['livestock','music','auction rhythm','riding','gardening'],quirk='He lets an animal settle before answering a question, which sometimes makes impatient customers reveal more than they intend.',belief='Judgment means noticing what a person would prefer you to overlook.',tension='He wants fair dealing but worries that challenging a respected seller will close the path to his own future.',fear='Being trusted to do the work and never trusted to speak about it.',want='Recognition for his judgment, savings toward a small holding, and a relationship he can approach at his own pace.',obstacle='Unequal influence in the yard and his reluctance to make an accusation without corroboration.',secret='He retained a legitimate copy of several inconsistent sale descriptions and has not yet decided who can help check them.',voice='Plain, observant, and quietly funny. His confidence is strongest when describing something he knows; affectionate words are fewer and deliberately chosen.',lines=['You can hear the sales pitch in a moment. First, I would look at how the animal is standing.','Cora says I need to project my voice. I explained that most of my regular audience prefers me quiet.','I am not saying the seller is dishonest. I am saying the descriptions change according to who is selling.','I would like to ask you to supper. I have been taking an unreasonable amount of time finding those words.'],romance='Reserved courtship, shared music and riding, thoughtful invitations, and increasing warmth through reliable familiarity. Low spice reflects his preferred expression, not an absence of adult desire.',boundary='No public teasing about his private pace, pressure to prove experience, or gifts that create an obligation. He wants explicit, unhurried agreement.',memories=['A difficult stock handling day went well because an older worker listened to his observation before giving orders.','The first time he called a practice sale clearly, Cora applauded as if it were a theater performance and then let him be embarrassed in peace.'],tasks=['inspect assigned livestock','prepare accurate sale descriptions','maintain yard and ownership records','assist scheduled auctions','coordinate loading under supervision','review accounts and calling practice'],anchors=[13,32,36],room='A valley room with a few carefully kept books, sale notes, a simple garden plan, and good clothes ready for an invitation he has not yet made.',ties=[(6,'employer and mentor','Adelaide values Isaac’s animal judgment but must learn to give him credit as well as responsibility.'),(10,'playful friendship','Cora helps Isaac practice speaking publicly and respects that private confidence develops differently.'),(24,'social friendship','Daisy and Isaac share ambition and enjoy ordinary outings without treating one another as projects.')]),
43:dict(
 bio='Ben is twenty-two and works as a checkweigher after entering mine employment as an adult. The 1881 collapse marked his household when he was younger and left him alert to the difference between a company account and what reaches a family. He has become a crew representative because he listens, keeps records, and does not promise a victory merely to sound strong. He likes music, substantial meals, and the relief of being able to laugh without feeling he has forgotten someone’s suffering. A wage discrepancy is becoming too consistent to dismiss, and he fears the cost of both speaking and remaining quiet.',look='Fair skin with an outdoor tan, hazel eyes, dark brown hair, and a strong face usually clean-shaven for work. Heavy work shirts, dark trousers, a brown coat, and a small family keepsake on a chain beneath his shirt.',traits=['steadfast','analytical','loyal','warm','burdened'],interests=['music','reading','cooking','local history','board games'],quirk='He writes down a figure before reacting to it, even when the number makes him angry.',belief='People cannot bargain fairly if they are denied an accurate account of their own work.',tension='He avoids heroic promises but still feels personally responsible for every household affected by a delay.',fear='Leading friends into a confrontation they cannot afford to sustain.',want='Honest weighing and pay, a credible mutual society, and room for a life beyond grievance.',obstacle='Incomplete records, company pressure, and a relief fund unable to support a long stoppage.',secret='He has enough evidence of a discrepancy to justify investigation but has let some colleagues assume he already has proof of deliberate fraud.',voice='Grounded and exact, with warmth outside formal meetings. He distinguishes a demand, a hope, and an established fact.',lines=['If you are asking about the pay, sit down. I would rather show you what we know than improve it in the telling.','Agnes says I am allowed to attend supper without bringing the mine. I am working on the skill.','I said there was a discrepancy. I should have stopped people when they began repeating it as a verdict.','It is good to be with someone who remembers I can enjoy a day as well as worry about it.'],romance='Warm mutual interest, shared meals and music, and honest vulnerability about responsibility. He wants affection that allows joy without requiring him to dismiss difficult work.',boundary='A partner is not expected to join a labor dispute, lend money, or disclose secrets to prove loyalty. Private relationships do not authorize workplace records.',memories=['A family meal after a hard year taught him that laughter could coexist with grief rather than betray it.','His first successful pay query ended quietly with a corrected figure, and he liked that nobody needed to become a hero.'],tasks=['record assigned ore weights','compare output and pay entries','maintain authorized copies','meet crew members about specific concerns','coordinate mutual-aid records','prepare qualified reports and shift handover'],anchors=[40,20,19],room='A boardinghouse room with a few books, a game board, family letters, and mine records kept in a closed case rather than spread over his bed.',ties=[(26,'professional alliance','Vera helps Ben distinguish a credible discrepancy from a claim his evidence cannot yet support.'),(18,'household ally','Agnes sees the consequences of wage delays and asks Ben for honest information instead of reassurance.'),(14,'community alliance','Ruth and Ben compare the way unpaid accounts and unpaid wages burden the same households.')]),
44:dict(
 bio='August is eighteen and works as cemetery keeper and an undertaker’s assistant under established local supervision. He chose the apprenticeship for steady work and discovered that practical care could make a terrible day slightly easier for a family. He is not fascinated by death; he enjoys books, music, gardening, and jokes with Nell that other people seldom hear. Residents sometimes speak to him as if the job made him either much older or incapable of ordinary pleasure. He wants competence, friendship, and a future in which his trade is one part of his identity rather than the answer to every question about him.',look='Fair skin, gray-blue eyes, light brown hair kept neatly trimmed, and a thoughtful, open face. Plain charcoal waistcoats, clean shirts, practical boots, and a green scarf on free days.',traits=['gentle','careful','wry','steadfast','private'],interests=['books','violin music','gardening','walking','drawing'],quirk='He brushes dust from a chair before offering it, even in a room that is already clean.',belief='Respect is often made of small practical things done without demanding recognition.',tension='He wants an ordinary social life but anticipates discomfort and withdraws before people can surprise him.',fear='Being treated as the town’s solemn symbol instead of a young adult with his own wants.',want='Complete his apprenticeship, make close friends, and enjoy a deliberate private romance if attraction is mutual.',obstacle='Social assumptions about his work and his habit of hiding behind their expectations.',secret='He has been taking music lessons privately because he wants one part of his life to begin with enjoyment rather than duty.',voice='Quiet, clear, and gently dry. He can be animated about books or music once the listener stops treating every remark as an expression of grief.',lines=['The public paths are open. If you are looking for someone in the register, I can help you ask properly.','Nell lent me a book with a very poor ending. We have decided to argue about it until one of us improves it.','I know what my work involves. It does not mean I want every conversation to begin there.','I would like to see you somewhere simply because we would enjoy being together.'],romance='Reserved, explicit courtship through walks, reading, music, and dependable private attention. He appreciates clear invitations and the freedom to answer without embarrassment.',boundary='No pressure to demonstrate maturity or experience. Active mourning, professional duties, and private preparation spaces are separate from romance.',memories=['A family once thanked him for remembering how a relative preferred a name pronounced; the detail changed how he understood his trade.','He played a short piece badly for Nell and found it easier to laugh because she had listened seriously first.'],tasks=['maintain public grounds and paths','prepare authorized service arrangements','assist the supervising undertaking service','maintain accurate memorial records','receive scheduled family inquiries','close the office and tend the grounds'],anchors=[22,33,37],room='A private bluff lodging room with books, a borrowed practice instrument, a small plant, and drawings of places unrelated to his work.',ties=[(17,'close quiet friendship','August and Nell exchange books and give one another room to be curious, uncertain, and funny.'),(36,'mentor and friend','Jonah supports August’s work without expecting his personal life to revolve around grief.'),(18,'community friendship','Agnes includes August in ordinary suppers and respects his wish to be invited as himself.')]),
45:dict(
 bio='Rafael is twenty and works the hotel’s evening desk, where attention to small preferences makes visitors feel that the town has already noticed them. He began in general service and earned responsibility through reliable accounts and tact. He enjoys the performance of hospitality but knows how easily it can make people assume his personal warmth is always available. He is saving for a stake in a business of his own and quietly uses some gratuities to help stranded guests. His generosity sometimes exceeds his means. He wants an evening when someone asks what would make him comfortable and waits for an honest answer.',look='Warm brown skin, dark eyes, thick black hair neatly combed back, and an expressive smile with one slightly crooked tooth. Dark waistcoats, clean white shirts, a burgundy necktie on duty, and a relaxed linen jacket outside work.',traits=['charming','attentive','resourceful','generous','privately restless'],interests=['music','travel stories','languages','cooking','theater'],quirk='He remembers where a guest likes a chair placed but has to think about where he wants to sit himself.',belief='Welcome is meaningful when it lets a person choose how much of themselves to reveal.',tension='He respects privacy while becoming emotionally invested in helping people whose difficulties he only partly understands.',fear='That everyone enjoys his company only because making it enjoyable is his job.',want='Build capital for independent work and a relationship in which hospitality becomes reciprocal.',obstacle='Modest pay, hidden relief expenses, and difficulty refusing an appealing request.',secret='He has reserved a cheap room for stranded travelers using his own gratuities, without a sustainable agreement from management.',voice='Warm, quick, and tactful, with humor that leaves the other person dignity. He becomes more openly playful when off duty and distinctly direct when a guest pressures staff.',lines=['I can offer a room, supper, and an opinion about the town. Only the first two have a fixed price.','Alma says I am welcome at the kitchen if I stop calling every burned crust an interesting local specialty.','I work here. That does not make another guest’s private business mine to give you.','Tonight I am not trying to make a guest feel welcome. I am asking whether you would like to be here with me.'],romance='Confident mutual flirtation, music, attentive dates, and a growing wish for care to travel both ways. He enjoys clear personal invitations outside his professional role.',boundary='Room access, guest records, and service never purchase intimacy. He will not accept a partner using jealousy to control whom he assists at work.',memories=['A traveler once returned only to thank him for not asking a question she could not bear to answer that night.','His first completely free evening in town ended at the Night Kitchen, where Alma told him to stop clearing dishes and sit down.'],tasks=['prepare the evening desk handover','assist arrivals and lodging requests','coordinate supper and guest needs','maintain private registers and accounts','resolve late practical problems','close his shift and arrange authorized coverage'],anchors=[12,11,21],room='A staff room at Calder House with a small travel map, well-kept clothes, a music booklet, and a private savings account recorded separately from hotel money.',ties=[(9,'late-shift friendship','Rafael and Alma share food and companionship after work, learning to stop serving each other long enough to rest.'),(13,'social friendship','Lottie enjoys Rafael’s observations about general visitor tastes, and he keeps individual guests’ private information out of the exchange.'),(38,'arrival coordination','Rafael and Nate help travelers manage real delays without inventing guarantees or disclosing unnecessary personal details.')]),
}
